Support nested morphism applications

Allow an enclosing model morphism to act on members at any nesting depth
through paths such as `f.X.T`. Explain path resolution with a surface
syntax example.

Name the morphism and member types in each application so their roles
are explicit throughout signature lookup and code generation.

Keep complex enum checks exhaustive so new variants require an explicit
decision, while allowing concise Option handling. Document this rule
and the preference for fewer branches and shallow nesting in AGENTS.md.
